    "intro_narrative": "The world ended not with a bang, but with a silent, toxic whisper. It has been twenty years since the Collapse, and the surface is nothing but a scorched wasteland scoured by irradiated winds. You are a Scavenger, desperate for a chance at survival. Rumors spoke of Sector Zero, an intact pre-war military bunker housing a legendary survival payload—a cache of pure water synthesizers and uncontaminated seeds. You have finally breached the facility's outer airlock, but the interior is a labyrinth of dead-end corridors, rusted technology, and automated lockdown protocols. Emergency lights flicker, casting long, menacing shadows across the ash-covered floors. Your Geiger counter clicks erratically, a constant reminder that time is running out. To reach the deepest level and secure the ultimate prize, you must power up dormant terminals, decipher the remnants of old-world technology, and bypass the bunker's complex security systems. Every terminal and mechanism is interconnected; missing a single step could seal you in this concrete tomb forever. Explore the ruins, trace the fragmented data pathways, and unlock the final payload before the radiation claims you.",
    "narrative_style": "post_apocalyptic"
  },
